// =====================================================================
// D05 - Suspicious Hidden PowerShell (Risk Scoring)
// =====================================================================
// MITRE ATT&CK : T1059.001 - Command and Scripting Interpreter: PowerShell
//                T1027.003 - Obfuscated Files or Information: Steganography
//                T1140     - Deobfuscate/Decode Files or Information
// Tactic       : Execution, Defense Evasion
// Severity     : High
// Data source  : Sysmon Event ID 1 (Process creation)
// Author       : Umang Udeshi
//
// Description:
//   Scores PowerShell command lines by counting suspicious options
//   (hidden window, execution policy bypass, non-interactive,
//   Invoke-Expression, encoded commands, Base64 decoding, image pixel
//   reading, web downloads). Alerts at 3 or more. One option alone can
//   be normal admin use; combinations rarely are.
//
// Tested against: OTRF APT29 Day 1 (196,081 events)
//   True positives : 1 (SCRANTON, 22:58:44 UTC, score 5/8 - steganography
//                    payload launched 2 seconds after the sdclt UAC bypass)
//   False positives: 0
//
// Known false positives:
//   Some management/deployment tools launch hidden PowerShell with
//   bypass. Review the parent process and allowlist verified tools.
//
// Mitigation:
//   Enable PowerShell script block logging and Constrained Language
//   Mode; application control (Essential Eight) to restrict scripts.
// =====================================================================
Apt29Raw
| where Channel == "Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" and EventID == 1
| where Image endswith "powershell.exe"
| extend CL = tolower(CommandLine)
| extend Score = toint(CL contains "hidden")
               + toint(CL contains "bypass")
               + toint(CL contains "-noni")
               + toint(CL contains "iex" or CL contains "invoke-expression")
               + toint(CL contains "-enc")
               + toint(CL contains "frombase64string")
               + toint(CL contains "getpixel")
               + toint(CL contains "downloadstring")
| where Score >= 3
| project EventTime, Hostname, User, Score, CommandLine
| order by EventTime asc
